      "value": "What'd be nice if it was possible for the player themselves to give other people nicknames as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-03T20:02:20.519Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, your VRChat username is the name shown on your nameplate. However, due to the fact that usernames have to be unique, people often have to add numbers, symbols, or other features into their username to make it unique. While account names should probably stay unique, the ability to set your own 'Nickname' that does not need to be unique would be a welcome addition.\nPlayers should still be able to check the specific username, perhaps through the quick menu or social tab, in order to prevent impersonation of other users, but nicknames would help allow players to set their display name what they're actually called, Such as 'James' instead of 'xX_James923_Xx'. It'd also allow players to set names as temporary jokes without having to commit to a full username change with a time limit on when it can be swapped.",
